## 🧪 Testing Requirements

### When to Add Tests

**Required for:**
- ✅ New API routes - Add to `__tests__/api/`
- ✅ New components - Add to `__tests__/components/`
- ✅ New utility functions - Add to `__tests__/lib/`
- ✅ Bug fixes - Add regression test

### Test Structure

Follow existing test patterns:

```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, afterEach } from 'vitest';

describe('Feature Name', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    // Setup
  });

  afterEach(() => {
    // Cleanup
  });

  it('should handle success case', async () => {
    // Arrange
    const input = { /* test data */ };
    
    // Act
    const result = await functionUnderTest(input);
    
    // Assert
    expect(result).toBeDefined();
    expect(result.status).toBe(200);
  });

  it('should handle error case', async () => {
    // Test error scenarios
  });
});
```

### Test Commands

- `pnpm test` - Run all tests (required before completion)
- `pnpm run test:watch` - Watch mode during development
- `pnpm run test:coverage` - Generate coverage report (for new features)

### Test Files Reference

- `__tests__/setup.ts` - Global test setup
- `__tests__/api/helpers/` - Test helpers and mocks
- `vitest.config.ts` - Test configuration

